---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Spend Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Spend Easy - Private Expense Tracker iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/spend-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Spend Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Spend%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Why doesn't Spend Easy connect to my bank?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">By design. We believe you shouldn't have to share your bank credentials with an expense tracking app. Manual entry gives you complete control over your financial data and keeps your banking information private.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I add an expense?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">On This month, type it in the bar at the bottom, like “Lunch 14.50” or “Groceries 82 yesterday”, and tap the arrow. Spend Easy shows what it read—amount, category and day—so you can check it and tap Add expense. For everything else, tap the pencil at the top right to open the full form.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I create my own categories?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Open the menu and tap Manage categories (or Settings → Categories) to add, edit, reorder or delete them, with your own name, icon and color.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I set up a budget?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Open the menu, tap Budgets, then Set a budget. Budgets can be daily, weekly or monthly. This month then leads with what’s left to spend. Turn on Budget alerts to get a notification when you reach the level you pick, and again if you go over.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Will my data sync between devices?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">No, Spend Easy stores all data locally on your device. This is intentional for privacy—your expense data never leaves your device. If you get a new phone, you can export your data to CSV and keep it as a record.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I export my expenses?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Open the menu, tap Settings, then Export as CSV. You get one file with every expense—date, category, note, amount, currency and repeat—that you can save, send or open in any spreadsheet app.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I track recurring expenses like subscriptions?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. In the full form, set Repeats to weekly, every 2 weeks, monthly, yearly or daily—or type it, like “Netflix 15.99 monthly”. Spend Easy adds the expense again on each date it repeats.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Which currency does Spend Easy use?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Your region’s currency, unless you pick another in Settings → Currency. Changing it changes how amounts are shown; it doesn’t convert them.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What happens if I delete the app?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">All your expense data will be deleted permanently. Since there's no cloud backup, we recommend exporting your data before uninstalling if you want to keep a record.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is there a subscription or premium version?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Spend Easy is free to download and use. All core features are available at no cost. No subscriptions, no hidden fees.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
